{
  "name": "CE-04 | Assemble Video (ffmpeg)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CE-04 | Assemble Video\n**Trigger:** every 10 minutes. Needs **ffmpeg + ffprobe** installed on the n8n machine and the *Execute Command* node enabled.\n\n**Flow**\n1. Picks one row with `status = Clips Ready`, sets it to `Assembling`.\n2. **ffprobe** reads the real length of every clip.\n3. A Code node writes an **SRT caption file** (4-word chunks timed across each clip) and builds the ffmpeg command.\n4. **ffmpeg step 1:** scales/pads every clip to 1080x1920 (9:16), 30 fps, stereo audio and joins them.\n   **ffmpeg step 2:** burns the captions in -> `final.mp4`.\n5. Uploads `final.mp4` to the *final videos* Drive folder and writes `drive_url` + `drive_file_id` to the sheet.\n6. Status `Video Ready` + email. **Watch it, then set status to `Publish`** (this is your second approval gate).\n\n**If ffmpeg fails:** the row becomes `Error` with the message in the `error` column. Fix the cause and set it back to `Clips Ready`.\n\n**Caption look:** edit `FontSize`, `MarginV` and `Outline` in the *Build SRT and Command* node.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 580,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "a8424e97-7351-5e21-a29a-2127914f3a63",
      "name": "Note - How this works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
